Spec: SystemDeleteCmd

Purpose:
  Back the `agent system delete` sub-command: resolve one @SystemInstance by namespace
    and name, publish it as the process-wide owner context and as the Rhai variable
    `instance`, inject the parsed CLI flags as the Rhai variable `args`, then hand the
    whole delete work to the Rhai modules `context` and `delete`. This file runs no
    delete stage itself: no directory scan, no resource teardown, no `status` write, no
    CR removal — it only prepares the engine and hands off.

References:
  ./install.sdd — the sibling install lane in the same module, which this file mirrors
    line-for-line. Known deltas, all deliberate-looking: @Parameters drops install's
    `--tag` (seven fields vs eight), the snippet imports the `delete` module instead of
    `install`, and @system::run routes this arm's failures to @process::exit(3) instead
    of @process::exit(1). `Depends on` deliberately shares install's shape.

Must:
  Execute these steps in this order, with nothing between them: build the interpreter,
    fetch the CR, publish context, inject `instance`, serialize and inject `args`,
    evaluate the snippet, return @Ok.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories in this
    order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the directory itself),
    `{script_dir}/system`, `{script_dir}/lib` — plain string interpolation of
    @std::path::Display, so a path argument ending in `/` doubles the separator;
    earlier entries win an `import`.
  @Script::new brings the full registration set — including @system_rhai_register, so
    the scripts hold `get_system_instance` and the whole @SystemInstance bridge plus
    the k8s, http, s3, jukebox and other instance-kind registrars — the same set the
    install lane gets.
  Fetch the CR with @SystemInstance::get taking clones of @Parameters.namespace and
    @Parameters.instance — one named-object read, never a list, watch, patch or delete.
  Publish the fetched CR twice from two clones: @context::set_system stores it as the
    process owner context, and @rhai::Scope::set_value on @Script::ctx binds the script
    variable named `instance`.
  Serialize @Parameters with @serde_json::to_value and inject it through
    @Script::set_dynamic as the script variable named `args`; the JSON object carries
    the declared snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`,
    `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `config_dir`, `controller_values` — seven keys, no
    `tag` — `controller_values` as a JSON string (its default renders `"{}"`, still a
    string, not an object) and the @PathBufs as path text.
  Evaluate the fixed four-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it:
    `import("context") as ctx; let context = ctx::run(instance, args);
    import("delete") as delete; delete::run(instance, context);` — `context` script
    first, its returned value becoming the `delete::run` second argument; `delete` runs
    second and last; the snippet's final statement ends with `;` so the resulting
    @rhai::Dynamic::UNIT is discarded by `let _ =` while a failed evaluation still
    propagates through `?`.
  Import lazily per statement as @rhai does: the `delete` module is only resolved when
    its `import` statement executes, so a missing `delete` module fails the eval only
    after `ctx::run` side effects have already run.
  Perform no cluster mutation of its own: no `status` write, no CR delete, no event —
    every teardown write happens inside the Rhai modules through the registered bridges;
    this file only reads the CR and returns @Ok with the CR it fetched untouched from
    this lane's perspective.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Treat an absent or already-deleted @SystemInstance as success: the @NotFound from
    @SystemInstance::get must propagate as a failure into the exit(3) lane — the fetch
    precedes any handoff, so absence tolerance cannot be assumed.
  Delete the @SystemInstance CR from Rust or write a finalizer or `status`, even after
    the snippet succeeded — closing out the delete belongs to the scripts and the
    controller, not to this handoff file.
  Interpret `controller_values` or gate on its contents.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver semantics and registration set,
    @Script::eval error lane, @Script::set_dynamic, @Script::ctx.
  /common/src/instancesystem.sdd — @SystemInstance and the @SystemInstance::get lookup
    this file awaits, and the registered bridges the scripts use for teardown writes.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @set_system store semantics and runtime preconditions.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error variants and @common::Result.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing (flags, envs, defaults in Accepts)
    and the derives behind the `args` JSON.
  /agent/scripts/system/context.rhai and /agent/scripts/system/delete.rhai — runtime
    handoff targets the snippet imports under the default `--script-dir`; owned instead
    by /agent/agent.sdd and unspecified here. The pre/post-uninstall dispatch
    (`delete_pre`, `delete_systems`, `delete_tofu`, `delete_crds`, `delete_post`) lives
    inside that `delete` module; this Rust file never names those stage modules.
  ./mod.rs — the only caller: @context::init_k8s call, then this arm's
    `unwrap_or_else` error lane (tracing text and @process::exit(3)).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct, also deriving @Debug, @Serialize and @Deserialize;
    mounted by @system::Commands::Delete in ./mod.rs; all seven fields private to this
    module, reached only by the derive code and by this file.
  @run — @pub async fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>; the sole
    caller is @system::run (delete dispatch arm).

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name `NAMESPACE`,
    @String, required (no `default_value`); the doc comment calls it the instance
    namespace to delete.
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name `INSTANCE`,
    @String, required.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`,
    value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; never read in this file beyond
    serialization into `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `/tmp/package`.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/scripts`.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name
    `CONFIG_DIR`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env
    `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default the
    two-character string `{}`.
  Shape delta vs ./install.sdd: no `tag` / `TAG` flag at all — seven fields, not eight.
  Implicit runtime precondition: a live tokio multi-thread runtime (from @main's
    @tokio::main), because @context::set_system crosses state with
    @tokio::task::block_in_place; @context::init_k8s already ran in @system::run before
    this file is entered and is inert either way.

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed eval snippet completes without a Rhai error — the @Dynamic
    value the snippet returns is discarded, never inspected.

Raises:
  @common::Error::KubeError from @SystemInstance::get when the API server rejects the
    lookup — including `NotFound` for an already-gone instance (Display `K8s error:
    ...`); the first fallible step, nothing published to context or scripts when it
    fails.
  @common::Error::SerializationError from the explicit @map_err when
    @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters) fails on the derives.
  @common::Error::Core (wrapping @vynil_core::Error::RhaiError, Display
    `Rhai script error: <rhai text>`) from the `?` on @Script::eval — a parse error in
    the fixed snippet, a failed `context` or `delete` import, or any parse error /
    thrown error inside those modules and whatever they import_run.
  The context-owned @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` surfaces through
    @SystemInstance::get when no kubeconfig or in-cluster configuration resolves.
  Panics from @context::set_system on a current-thread runtime or no runtime at all
    (contract in /common/src/context.sdd), not catchable by the parent `?` lane.

Handles:
  @Err lane owned by the caller — @system::run logs the ./mod.rs literal format string
    `Deleting a package failed with: {e:}` through @tracing::error and calls
    @process::exit(3); code `3` is this arm's delete-specific exit, distinct from
    install's `1`. This file logs nothing and never exits, so a failed delete leaves no
    status marker written by this lane.
  Failed lookup or failed eval after `@set_system` already ran — the process context
    keeps the @VynilContext::SystemInstance variant for the remaining process lifetime
    (which ends in the exit(3)).
  Already-gone instance — no absence-tolerance branch: the hard @KubeError above is
    the whole behaviour; no script ever runs to do an idempotent no-op delete.
  Half-deleted instance — no branch on `status`, finalizers or the contents of
    `package_dir` here: a rerun refetches the CR and replays both modules; stage
    skipping (the is_dir and `tofu` guards) is `delete.rhai`'s script-side contract.
  Absent resolver directories — the four search paths are never existence-checked at
    construction; the failure only lands later as the @common::Error::Core import error
    if no search dir holds `context.rhai` / `delete.rhai`.
  Flags with no local reader (`vynil_namespace`, `controller_values`) — their only
    observable use is the `args` JSON the scripts consume.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover all five Scenarios with tests; no test invokes this @run —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs exercises the Rhai modules directly, bypassing
      this Rust lane.
  [?] Cross-lane shape drift with ./install.sdd: the service- and tenant-kind delete
      lanes (/agent/src/service/delete.rs, /agent/src/tenant/delete.rs) carry
      `-t`/`--template-dir` and `--agent-image` like their install twins, while system
      delete is exactly the seven-flag system shape minus `--tag`. Decide whether the
      system kind genuinely needs neither and the three hand-copied shapes stay.
  [?] Delete of an already-gone instance is a hard failure: @SystemInstance::get runs
      first, so a retried delete Job whose CR was removed meanwhile (controller
      cleanup, or an earlier partial run) exits 3 instead of converging silently.
      Confirm the controller never re-dispatches this Job after the CR is gone, or
      decide whether @NotFound on the delete lane becomes a silent @Ok.
  [?] `vynil_namespace` and `controller_values` are typed and (for `vynil_namespace`)
      required, yet this file never reads them — their contract lives only in the
      script-side `args` JSON. Same open point as ./install.sdd: confirm the
      requiredness belongs to the Rhai contract or relax the flags.
  [?] `controller_values` reaches scripts as a JSON string even when it holds `{}`,
      so every consumer must decode it. Decide whether this file should pre-parse it
      into an object (mirrors ./install.sdd).
  [?] The eval @Dynamic is discarded (`let _ =`): confirm no `delete::run` return
      value may ever gate success, closing a delete Job that half-failed.
  [?] @Deserialize on @Parameters has no deserialization site in the workspace (the
      Rust lane only serializes it toward scripts). Decide whether the derive stays.

Done when:
  The five Scenarios hold under tests pinning resolver-path order, the seven-key
    `args` JSON with no `tag` and `controller_values` as a string, and the
    error-to-exit(3) lane including the already-gone-CR hard failure.

Scenario: full run hands off in order
  Given all required flags supplied (by flag or env), an existing namespaced
    @SystemInstance named by @Parameters.instance, and `context.rhai` plus
    `delete.rhai` resolvable under `{script_dir}/system`
  When @run is awaited
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`, `[config]`,
    `[script]/system`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And before the eval, the process owner context is the system variant (via
    @set_system) and `instance` and `args` are bound, `args` carrying the seven
    snake_case keys with `controller_values` as a JSON string
  Then the `context` module's `run` executes before the `delete` module's `run`,
    receiving (`instance`, `args`), and the resulting `context` value is what
    `delete::run` receives
  And @run returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was, having performed no
    cluster write of its own

Scenario: absent or already-gone CR fails before any handoff
  Given no @SystemInstance exists at that namespace/name — never created, or removed
    by an earlier delete run or by the controller
  When @run is awaited
  Then the @SystemInstance::get `?` returns @Err(@common::Error::KubeError)
  And @set_system never ran (context stays @VynilContext::None), `instance`/`args` were
    never injected and neither module ran
  And @system::run logs `Deleting a package failed with: K8s error: ...` at
    @tracing::error level and exits the process 3

Scenario: missing required flag never reaches Rust logic
  Given `--instance` omitted and `INSTANCE` unset in the environment — same lane for
    `--namespace` / `NAMESPACE` and `--vynil-namespace` / `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`
  When the binary parses @Parameters
  Then clap exits with its usage error before @run starts — no interpreter, no cluster
    read, and the exit-3 delete lane is never entered

Scenario: delete module missing after context already ran
  Given a valid @SystemInstance, `context.rhai` resolvable in a search dir, and no
    `delete.rhai` resolvable in any of the four resolver directories
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then `ctx::run` and its side effects execute first, then @Script::eval returns
    @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed `Rhai script error:`)
  And the process context still holds the system variant when the exit(3) lane fires

Scenario: rerun over a half-deleted instance
  Given a @SystemInstance whose `{package_dir}/systems`, `tofu` and `crds` stage
    content was already torn down by a previous delete run
  When @run is invoked again with the same flags
  Then the CR is refetched and both modules replay from the top — this file skips
    nothing based on `status` or on the stage directories, whose re-check is
    `delete.rhai`'s script-side contract
